---
// VeloPad Privacy Policy (/products/velopad/velopad-privacy)
// Linked from the VeloPad product page and the Google Play listing.
// Plain-language version: every disclosure from the original is kept; implementation details were dropped.

import BaseLayout from '../../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/sections/PageHero.astro';

const sections = [
  { id: 's1', title: '1. The short version' },
  { id: 's2', title: '2. What the Android app uses' },
  { id: 's3', title: '3. What the PC client uses' },
  { id: 's4', title: '4. Android permissions' },
  { id: 's5', title: '5. What VeloPad does not collect' },
  { id: 's6', title: '6. Outside services' },
  { id: 's7', title: '7. Where your data is kept' },
  { id: 's8', title: "8. Children's privacy" },
  { id: 's9', title: '9. Sharing' },
  { id: 's10', title: '10. Your choices' },
  { id: 's11', title: '11. Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 's12', title: '12. Contact' },
];

const permissions = [
  {
    name: 'INTERNET',
    reason:
      'To talk to your PC over your local network, and, for Pro subscribers, to check the subscription with our verification service.',
  },
  { name: 'ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE', reason: 'To check that a network connection is available before connecting.' },
  { name: 'ACCESS_WIFI_STATE', reason: "To read your phone's local network address so it can connect to your PC." },
  { name: 'CHANGE_WIFI_MULTICAST_STATE', reason: 'To find your PC on your local network automatically.' },
  { name: 'HIGH_SAMPLING_RATE_SENSORS', reason: 'To read the motion sensors quickly enough for smooth aiming.' },
  { name: 'VIBRATE', reason: 'To give a small vibration when you press a button.' },
];

// Shared class strings
const h2 = 'scroll-mt-24 mb-4 font-heading text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink md:text-[28px]';
const h3 = 'font-heading text-lg font-semibold text-ink';
const body = 'flex flex-col gap-4 text-ink-mid';
const item = 'flex flex-col gap-2 border-t border-line-strong pt-5';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="VeloPad Privacy Policy — Blue Wave Horizon"
  description="VeloPad does not collect your personal data. Here is what the app uses, where it goes and why, in plain language."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="VeloPad" title="Privacy Policy">
    <p class="text-ink-mid">
      Last updated: November 17, 2026 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Developer: Blue Wave Horizon Ltd. &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; App
      package: <code class="rounded bg-alt px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">com.bwh.velopad</code>
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="wrap flex flex-col gap-10 pb-20 sm:pb-28 lg:flex-row lg:items-start lg:gap-20">
    <nav
      class="flex flex-col border-y border-line-strong py-5 text-[15px] lg:sticky lg:top-24 lg:w-[280px] lg:shrink-0 lg:border-y-0 lg:py-0"
      aria-label="On this page"
    >
      <p class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.06em] text-ink-mid">On this page</p>
      {
        sections.map((s) => (
          <a
            href={`#${s.id}`}
            class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center text-ink-mid transition-colors duration-150 hover:text-ink"
          >
            {s.title}
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </nav>

    <div class="flex min-w-0 max-w-[720px] flex-col gap-14 [overflow-wrap:anywhere] lg:flex-1">
      <!-- 1 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s1" class={h2}>1. The short version</h2>
        <div class={body}>
          <p>VeloPad comes in two parts: an Android app that acts as the controller, and a PC client that runs on Windows, Linux or macOS and receives its input.</p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">VeloPad does not collect your personal data, and it does not sell or share data with anyone.</strong>
            Your movements, taps and layouts travel only between your phone and your PC, over your own local network.
          </p>
          <p>
            The app reaches the internet in two cases only: to confirm a VeloPad Pro subscription, and, on the PC, to check
            for updates. Both are explained below.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 2 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s2" class={h2}>2. What the Android app uses</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 text-ink-mid">
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>Motion sensors</h3>
            <p>The app reads your phone's gyroscope and accelerometer to turn its movement into aiming on your PC. The readings go straight to your PC over your local network and are discarded as soon as they're sent. They never reach us or anyone else.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>Touch input</h3>
            <p>Your taps, swipes and stick movements on the on-screen controller are sent to your PC the same way, and are not kept.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>Local network details</h3>
            <p>To find your PC without you typing in an address, the app looks up your phone's local network address and the addresses of VeloPad PCs on the same network. These are used only to connect, are not sent anywhere else, and are forgotten when you close the app.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>Settings and controller layouts</h3>
            <p>Your settings and saved layouts are stored on your phone. If you choose to sync layouts with your PC, they move directly between the two over your local network and never leave it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>VeloPad Pro subscription check <span class="font-normal text-muted">(Pro subscribers only)</span></h3>
            <p>When you subscribe to VeloPad Pro, Google Play gives the app a purchase code. To confirm your subscription is active, the app sends that code, along with the app's package name, over a secure connection to our verification service on Google Cloud (Firebase).</p>
            <p>The service checks the code with Google Play and sends back a signed confirmation that holds only your plan and when it expires. It does not store the code or anything else. Your name, email address, device ID and other personal details are never sent.</p>
            <p>The confirmation is stored encrypted on your phone so the app doesn't need to go online every time it starts. When your phone connects to your PC, it passes the confirmation over your local network so the PC can check your Pro status offline.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 3 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s3" class={h2}>3. What the PC client uses</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 text-ink-mid">
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>Input from your phone</h3>
            <p>The PC client listens on your local network for your phone. What it receives is turned into controller, mouse or keyboard input on your PC. None of it is stored or passed on.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>Settings and controller layouts</h3>
            <p>Your settings and layouts are saved on your computer and are never uploaded. Syncing with your phone happens directly over your local network.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>Update check</h3>
            <p>When you open the PC client, or check for updates yourself, it asks GitHub for the latest version number and download link. No personal information or device identifiers are sent. You can block this request in your firewall and VeloPad will still work.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>VeloPad Pro check</h3>
            <p>The PC client checks the Pro confirmation it receives from your phone by itself, offline. It never goes online to check your subscription.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 4 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s4" class={h2}>4. Android permissions</h2>
        <div class={body}>
          <p>These are the permissions the Android app asks for, and why.</p>
          <dl class="flex flex-col border-b border-line-strong">
            {
              permissions.map((p) => (
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 border-t border-line-strong py-4 sm:flex-row sm:gap-6">
                  <dt class="sm:w-[250px] sm:shrink-0">
                    <code class="rounded bg-alt px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-ink">{p.name}</code>
                  </dt>
                  <dd>{p.reason}</dd>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </dl>
          <p>VeloPad does not ask for your location. Reading your network details shows only your local address on your home network, not where you are.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 5 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s5" class={h2}>5. What VeloPad does not collect</h2>
        <div class={body}>
          <ul class="flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 pl-6">
            <li>Your name, email address or account details</li>
            <li>Your Google account information</li>
            <li>Device identifiers, such as your advertising ID or Android ID</li>
            <li>Your location</li>
            <li>Your contacts, calendar or anything else stored on your phone</li>
            <li>Analytics, diagnostics or crash reports</li>
            <li>Anything for advertising or marketing</li>
            <li>Which games you play or how you use the controller</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The app contains no analytics, advertising or crash-reporting tools.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 6 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s6" class={h2}>6. Outside services</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 text-ink-mid">
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>Google Play</h3>
            <p>Google Play handles VeloPad Pro payments under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-link underline underline-offset-2">Google's Privacy Policy</a>. We only receive the purchase code described above. Your card details and billing address never reach us.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>Google Cloud (Firebase)</h3>
            <p>Our subscription check runs on Google Cloud, in the United States (us-central1). Google may record the internet (IP) address the request comes from in its standard server logs. Those logs are managed by Google under Google Cloud's data processing terms, and we don't control them.</p>
          </div>
          <div class={item}>
            <h3 class={h3}>GitHub</h3>
            <p>The PC client's update check goes to GitHub, under the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" class="text-link underline underline-offset-2">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>. No personal information is sent.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 7 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s7" class={h2}>7. Where your data is kept</h2>
        <div class={body}>
          <p>Everything VeloPad stores stays on your own devices. We keep no user data in the cloud.</p>
          <ul class="flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 pl-6">
            <li>On your phone, settings and layouts are protected by Android's normal app storage. Your Pro confirmation is also encrypted, with the key held in Android's secure key store.</li>
            <li>On your PC, settings and layouts are ordinary files in the VeloPad folder, protected by your computer's own security.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 8 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s8" class={h2}>8. Children's privacy</h2>
        <div class={body}>
          <p>VeloPad is not aimed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. Because VeloPad doesn't collect personal data from anyone, this includes children.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 9 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s9" class={h2}>9. Sharing</h2>
        <div class={body}>
          <p>We do not sell, trade, rent or share personal data. The only times VeloPad sends anything outside your home network are:</p>
          <ul class="flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 pl-6">
            <li>the VeloPad Pro subscription check, for Pro subscribers only (section 2)</li>
            <li>the PC client's update check with GitHub (section 3)</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Neither includes personal information about you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 10 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s10" class={h2}>10. Your choices</h2>
        <div class={body}>
          <p>We don't hold personal data about you, so there's nothing for us to access, correct or delete. You stay in control of what's on your devices:</p>
          <ul class="flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 pl-6">
            <li>Uninstalling the Android app removes all its settings and layouts from your phone.</li>
            <li>Deleting the PC client's profiles folder and settings file removes everything it stored on your computer.</li>
            <li>You can cancel VeloPad Pro at any time in the Google Play Store. The app picks up the change the next time it checks.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 11 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s11" class={h2}>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <div class={body}>
          <p>If this policy changes, we'll post the new version here with a new date, and mention significant changes in the app's release notes. If you keep using VeloPad after an update, you accept the revised policy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 12 -->
      <div>
        <h2 id="s12" class={h2}>12. Contact</h2>
        <div class={body}>
          <p>Questions about this policy? Get in touch:</p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">Blue Wave Horizon Ltd.</strong><br />
            <a href="mailto:hello@bluewavehz.com" class="text-link underline underline-offset-2">hello@bluewavehz.com</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-line">
    <div class="wrap py-8">
      <a href="/products/velopad" class="text-link-arrow">&larr; Back to VeloPad</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
